    <string name="presentation_archive_disclosure">Selected information from permitted notifications that may be useful later is stored locally long term, including from silent notifications: up to 100,000 facts and a 128 MiB database, without automatic age-based deletion. This information remains a claim made by its source, not a confirmed profile answer. Raw notifications are separate and are kept for only seven days by default. The fact archive is not part of the Hans backup and is not native Codex memory. Forgetting items in this archive does not delete earlier chats or Codex memories derived from them.</string>
